Ladybird now has an element that inherits a text shadow reading
currentcolor take its parent’s computed shadow: absolute lengths,
resolved against the parent’s font, with currentcolor kept for the
child to resolve. Blink, WebKit, and Gecko all compute and inherit
shadows that way: Blink’s StyleBuilderConverter::ConvertShadow()
computes each length with ComputeLength() and keeps StyleColor::
CurrentColor(), WebKit’s Style::TextShadow holds computed Length<>
values and a Style::Color, and Gecko’s computed SimpleShadow is a
GenericSimpleShadow of computed Color and Length values.
